  "sourceAssessment": {
    "basis": [
      "jinshu:053:s0034–s0035 names 壽妻賈午 refusing Guo Huai’s proposed Han-daughter marriage and choosing Wang Yan’s younger daughter. zizhitongjian:083:s0128–s0129 repeats the same wife, husband, proposed marriage and refusal; these identify one woman across the two records.",
      "jinshu:031:s0530 names 后妹午; s0571 identifies 韓壽 as 妹夫, while s0579–s0581 pair 午 with 趙粲 in the empress’s plot. zizhitongjian:083:s0131–s0135 repeats Guo Huai’s deathbed warning naming 趙粲、賈午 and their plot. These distinctive family and narrative links connect the Jin031 member.",
      "jinshu:031:s0599 lists 趙粲、賈午 among those punished when the empress falls; zizhitongjian:083:s0243–s0262 gives the corresponding coup and s0260 sends 趙粲、賈午 to 暴室. The second Tongjian record is this same named woman, not a new homonym."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Read all 124 Chinese source units in nine complete governing blocks, all four current singleton records, 23 owned claims, 19 mentions and one inbound spouse claim; both English fields read for every owned and inbound source anchor.",
      "Jin053 source106 preserves the explicit wife identification in the literal field, although idiomatic English uses her name alone. Chinese controls identity; English abbreviation does not create another person. All aliases, female/family roles, AD272–300 hints, twelve-year age and execution assertions remain unchanged; no new date is inferred.",
      "All four complete canonical memberships are included in one fresh current-source merge covering all three owned pairs. No archived verdict or approval is restored."
    ]
